,"current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"yes","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"no","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"none","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] In AC7 (or the script docstring), name the standard drift-detection prior art (native `terraform plan -refresh-only` / Terraform Cloud drift / driftctl) and state why it structurally cannot catch this class — those tools compare state to the cloud control plane, which reported this volume `in-use`, while the gap is guest-side (never mounted) — establishing the state-vs-guest-runtime join as the actual novelty.","cohort":["T1"],"criteria":["T1"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.8,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Web search confirms the mainstream prior art for 'declared but diverged' is control-plane drift detection: native `terraform plan`/`-refresh-only`, HashiCorp 'Terraform Cloud Adds Drift Detection', and driftctl (per awesome-tf).","The repo already ships this category: .github/workflows/terraform-drift.yml runs `terraform plan (fail on drift)` (.github/mechanism-baseline.json:355).","The plan engages that workflow only on IAM grounds ('that workflow assumes the rebar-terraform-plan OIDC role, which is ReadOnlyAccess + kms:Decrypt ... ssm:SendCommand is a WRITE action absent'), not on the substantive point that a control-plane drift check would report this volume HEALTHY: AWS confirmed it 